name: Missing experimental Go scanner retains an actionable failure and no clean evidence
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/govulncheck_missing.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: options govulncheck:scan
require-live-snap: 25 Experimental | experimental-options
expect: Target
keys: Escape
submit: logs
submit: run govulncheck:scan {}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/govulncheck_missing.py @TMP_TARGET @ART failed
paste-file: @ART/failed-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Outcome · failed | failed-receipt
expect: binary not found
expect: go install
resize: 160x48
live-snap: failure-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: failure-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: failure-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: failure-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: failure-40x12
expect: failed
ask: Across six sizes, can the operator identify the failed action and use the visible reading controls to reach its missing-dependency cause?
resize: 120x36
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Finding review completeness does not describe repository coverage. | empty-report
expect: REPORT
expect: 0 findings
expect: Finding review completeness does not describe repository coverage.
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/govulncheck_missing.py @TMP_TARGET @ART report
ask: Does the empty Report avoid treating the unavailable experimental scanner as successful clean coverage or spending model capacity?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/failed-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Outcome · failed | restarted-failure
expect: binary not found
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/govulncheck_missing.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain the failure, recovery action and unchanged source with no scanner process, Go loading or model request?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
